; The region fixpoint is bounded by the program, not by a constant.
;
; `rgnRounds` walks every `fn` until no fact moves, with the bound at
; `(vecLen decls) + 1`. Before 2026-09-17 the bound was a bare 40, and
; both outcomes answered 0, so `restrictNoEscape` could not tell a
; claim the walk PROVED from one it ABANDONED - and it read the
; abandoned one as a silence, which is what a proven claim looks
; like.
;
; MEASURED before that fix, on this exact shape: a chain of depth 38
; was refused with AX3049 and a chain of depth 39 was ACCEPTED IN
; SILENCE, on a leaf that provably stores a fresh allocation into its
; parameter.
;
; DECLARATION ORDER IS WHY THIS HID. `rgnPass` walks the declaration
; list in order, so when a callee is declared ABOVE its caller the facts
; travel the whole chain in one pass and any depth converges in two.
; This file declares each callee BELOW its caller, so exactly one level
; propagates per pass - past the old cap, within the new bound.
; Written the other way round, this same program is refused at any
; depth, under either bound.
;
; So, since the fix: `top` gets AX3049, refuted - the claim is
; disproven, through `f42` - and `topStrict` gets AX3049 too, because
; there is nothing unproven left for `strict` to refuse.
(import Vec)
(import Str)

;@axiom:restrict(no-escape)
(:: top (-> (Vec String) String Int))
(fn (top v x)
  (f42 v x))

;@axiom:restrict(no-escape, strict)
(:: topStrict (-> (Vec String) String Int))
(fn (topStrict v x)
  (f42 v x))

(:: f42 (-> (Vec String) String Int))
(fn (f42 v x)
  (f41 v x))

(:: f41 (-> (Vec String) String Int))
(fn (f41 v x)
  (f40 v x))

(:: f40 (-> (Vec String) String Int))
(fn (f40 v x)
  (f39 v x))

(:: f39 (-> (Vec String) String Int))
(fn (f39 v x)
  (f38 v x))

(:: f38 (-> (Vec String) String Int))
(fn (f38 v x)
  (f37 v x))

(:: f37 (-> (Vec String) String Int))
(fn (f37 v x)
  (f36 v x))

(:: f36 (-> (Vec String) String Int))
(fn (f36 v x)
  (f35 v x))

(:: f35 (-> (Vec String) String Int))
(fn (f35 v x)
  (f34 v x))

